 Implicated in combined oxidative phosphorylation deficiency 42. [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"O43716","text":"Structural subunit of the mitochondrial Glu-tRNA(Gln) amidotransferase complex GatCAB. GatCAB allows the formation of correctly charged Gln-tRNA(Gln) through the transamidation of misacylated Glu-tRNA(Gln) in the mitochondria (PubMed:19805282). The reaction takes place in the presence of glutamine and ATP through an activated gamma-phospho-Glu-tRNA(Gln) (By similarity). This subunit probably forms a belt that wraps around the interface of the catalytic subunits A and B to stabilize the complex (Probable)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}